  THE SHAPE-LOCK ALGEBRA (H055 chain internal fixed points):
    gamma = (2+n)/n  =>  distribution exponent 2/(1-gamma) = -n  (exact, all n)
      n = 1.000 -> gamma =  3.000 -> dM/dg exponent = -1.000 (= -n, exact)
      n = 1.200 -> gamma =  2.667 -> dM/dg exponent = -1.200 (= -n, exact)
      n = 1.596 -> gamma =  2.253 -> dM/dg exponent = -1.596 (= -n, exact)
      n = 2.000 -> gamma =  2.000 -> dM/dg exponent = -2.000 (= -n, exact)
      n = 3.161 -> gamma =  1.633 -> dM/dg exponent = -3.161 (= -n, exact)
    the kernel's own deep RAR slope (G183 family): 1 - n/4
      n = 2.000 (the phantom, locked): deep slope 0.500 -- the quadratic's 1/2
      vs the measured per-galaxy deep slope 0.601 +- 0.031 (G158): z = (+0.10)/0.031 = +3.3 sigma
      the family member that reproduces 0.601 EXACTLY: n = 4(1-0.601) = 1.596 -> gamma = 2.253 (NOT the phantom 2.0)
    the n = 2 amplitude-channel degeneracy: deep a0_eff = a0^(n/2) g_N^(1-n/2);
      at n = 2: a0_eff = a0 EXACTLY for every scale -- the phantom-locked loop is
      a0-BLIND: every a0 is a fixed point on the n = 2 ridge, no determination.

